  data:  # e831
    kind: work_item  # e831
    title: "SCIP-import Symbols carry bare origin='scip' with no AnalysisRun join (finish synthetic:F1 for the SCIP pass)"  # e831
    status: todo_soft  # e831
    priority: 3  # e831
    parent:  # e831
    tags:  # e831
    - classification_axes  # e831
    - analysis_quality  # e831
    isbefore: []  # e831
    duplicate_of: []  # e831
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e831
    pr_ref:  # e831
    description: "Split-off from WI-kadop (ADR-0044). The SCIP-index import (rust-analyzer) sets Symbol.origin='scip' (bare) at scip/index.py:202 and Edge.origin='scip' at scip/edges.py:125 / scip/calls.py:178. synthetic:F1 gave the two orchestrator-level synthesizers (orchestrator_file_symbol_synthesis / boundary_external_symbol_synthesis) a real AnalysisRun whose pass_id is the origin value + threaded origin_run_id so nodes join. The SCIP pass was NOT given the same treatment: rust-analyzer translate.py:175 DOES create a scip AnalysisRun (pass_id=make_pass_id('rust-scip-translate')) and threads run_id to edges/calls, but (a) the SYMBOLS (scip_index_to_symbols) don't receive run_id at all, and (b) both symbols and edges use the bare literal 'scip' as origin instead of the run's real pass_id. So SCIP-sourced Symbols have no node->AnalysisRun provenance join. Fix: thread run_id into scip_index_to_symbols, and set origin=[the rust-scip-translate pass_id] on scip symbols + edges (replacing bare 'scip'); ensure that pass_id is in all_known_pass_ids; update the consumer rust_analyzer/analyzer.py:115 (any('scip' in edge.origin)). Then 'scip' can be removed from catalog._SYNTHETIC_PASS_IDS. Off-self-corpus (rust-analyzer SCIP path only) — validate via the rust-analyzer package tests, not self-analysis. Cross-package (touches hypergumbo-lang-rust-analyzer)."  # e831
    fields: {}  # e831
- op: discuss  # 9ddd
  at: '2026-09-17T20:06:03Z'  # 9ddd
  by: agent  # 9ddd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9ddd
  clock: 2  # 9ddd
  nonce: 9ddd  # 9ddd
  message: "CONFIRMED AND SIZED, 2026-09-17 at 06699b1d91. This row's statement holds\nexactly as written, and the count is 669.\n\nHYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 survey of ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns:\n\n    nodes carrying origin=['scip']            669  (53% of all 1255 nodes)\n    of those, origin_run_id == ''             669  (ALL of them)\n    resulting Symbol.origin_run_id violations 669\n\n    kinds: local 500, method 79, variable 47, class 25, namespace 18\n\nTHE EDGE HALF IS WORSE AND IS THE SAME DEFECT. 637 scip edges carry a\nFABRICATED origin_run_id -- a well-formed UUID matching no AnalysisRun --\nbecause Edge.__post_init__ hard-raises on empty (WI-higap) and translate.py\nsatisfies the guard by constructing an AnalysisRun purely to harvest its\nexecution_id, then discarding it. Symbol has no such guard, which is why this\nside is honestly empty and the edge side is a convincing lie.\n\nROOT CAUSE AND FIX filed as WI-didag: the rust-analyzer success path returns\nAnalysisResult(symbols, edges) with no run=, and the run_id parameter that\nexists on translate_scip_to_hg is unreachable from production because\ntry_analyze_with_rust_analyzer does not thread it.\n\nCONSEQUENCE FOR THIS ROW: \"finish synthetic:F1 for the SCIP pass\" is likely not\nthe right fix. These symbols do not need a SYNTHETIC run -- the pass genuinely\nran and should have emitted a real AnalysisRun. Threading the real one closes\nthis row and the 637 edges together. Recommend re-pointing from synthetic:F1 to\n\"consume the real run once WI-didag threads it\". No status change made."  # 9ddd
