- op: discuss  # 1465
  at: '2026-09-17T20:51:13Z'  # 1465
  by: agent  # 1465
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1465
  clock: 4  # 1465
  nonce: '1465'  # 1465
  message: "FIXED in f685e584ef, closed on this row's own repro.\n\nTHE STATEMENT: \"SCIP-import Symbols carry bare origin='scip' with no\nAnalysisRun join.\" Measured before the fix on\nHYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER=1 survey of ~/whole_bunch_of_repos/aardvark-dns:\n669 nodes carrying origin=['scip'], ALL with origin_run_id == ''.\n\nAFTER: 669 nodes, 0 with a dangling or empty origin_run_id. Every one joins\nto the rust_analyzer AnalysisRun, which is now present in analysis_runs.\nSymbol.origin_run_id violations 669 -> 0.\n\nWHERE THE STAMP LANDED, and why not where this row proposed. The title says\n\"finish synthetic:F1 for the SCIP pass\". That would have been the wrong fix:\nthese symbols never needed a SYNTHETIC run, because the pass genuinely ran and\nshould have emitted a real AnalysisRun. It now does (WI-didag), and\ntranslate_scip_to_hg stamps the symbols from the caller's run_id at the point\nof minting.\n\nDeliberately NOT relying on the orchestrator's WI-mosil backstop, which fills\nonly empty ids and only inside run_behavior_map: translate_scip_to_hg is an\nexported function, and a library caller using it directly would have kept the\nbare symbols. Stamping at the source covers both.\n\nThe edge half of the same defect -- 637 edges carrying a FABRICATED run id\nrather than an empty one, because Edge.__post_init__ hard-raises on empty and\nSymbol does not -- is fixed by the same change and is written up on WI-didag.\n\nFull suite 4835 passed; ratchet 667 (delta +0)."  # 1465
